  "question": "Can the official PKU platform current search backend close a stable article identity/detail route for 《五石斋文史札记》(二十八), and does the detail page's own ArticleFile route expose the primary text/file?",
  "answer": "Yes for stable article identity/detail metadata; no for retrievable ArticleFile. The official PKU search page source emits POST /Search/SearchArticleByElasticsearch, its CSRF token, Title-field query structure, 100/Page UI, and source-emitted detail template /article/info?aid={{item.id}}. Executing that source-defined contract with the title 五石斋文史札记 returns all 37 series records and exactly one installment-28 match: id 286663046, 邓之诚/邓瑞, 中国典籍与文化 2008(03), pp.121-129, volumeIssueId 12482306. The source-returned detail URL /article/info?aid=286663046 returns HTTP 200 and displays the exact title and page range. Its search record says hasFullText=true while isFileExist=false and fulltextFId=null. The detail page itself source-emits /Article/DownLoad?id=286663046&&type=ArticleFile; following that exact route without login or guessed IDs returns HTTP 200 application/json with succeeded=false and errors=文件不存在. Therefore the current stable detail route is closed, but Fulltext/hasFullText must not be equated with a currently retrievable article file or primary journal text.",
